<title>RUSSIA: Yeltsin vows to ignore Duma opposition to reform.</title>
<headline>Yeltsin vows to ignore Duma opposition to reform.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian President Boris Yeltsin said on Friday he would ignore opposition in parliament to his market reforms and press ahead with them regardless.</p>
<p>&quot;Regretfully, the deputies have not supported the decision which is needed and have been afraid to shoulder responsibility for these painful but vitally important measures,&quot; Yeltsin said in a radio address. &quot;We will do all that is necessary with regard to this decision.&quot;</p>
</text>
